The shared tile candidate reuses operand threadgroup storage for the
post-compute output tail, with an explicit barrier before aliasing. F32
expressions, tile shapes and fixed ggml layout attribution are unchanged.

The IQ2 scalar lane experiment adapts the 32-value group ownership and scale
factoring from ggml/src/ggml-metal/kernels/mul_mv.metal at revision
555d1ec9daa4564cb06adb39c469acfdcd1d1e93, covered by the MIT notice above.

The F32 packed attention candidate adapts eight-query/64-key matrix tiling
and online softmax rescaling from ggml/src/ggml-metal/kernels/fa.metal at
revision 555d1ec9daa4564cb06adb39c469acfdcd1d1e93, under the MIT notice above.
The implementation retains F32 query staging and the exact QSA mask.

The generic-path matrix-vector kernels in kernels/generic.metal (mv_q4k,
mv_q6k, mv_q4_0) adapt kernel_mul_mv_q4_K_f32_impl, kernel_mul_mv_q6_K_f32_impl
and mul_vec_q_n_f32_impl from ggml/src/ggml-metal/kernels/mul_mv.metal at
ggml-org/llama.cpp revision 9b56ccf00d755b0bf780140f6352a67db1ac0378, under the
MIT notice above. The F16 and F32 vector kernels share that structure, and the
prefill GEMM kernels in the same file (gemm_q4k, gemm_q6k, gemm_q4_0) follow
kernel_mul_mm from the same revision.

The material below also comes from ggml-org/llama.cpp revision
9b56ccf00d755b0bf780140f6352a67db1ac0378, under the MIT notice above:
- src/spm.rs ports the SentencePiece and gemma4 tokenizers from
  src/llama-vocab.cpp.
- src/generic.rs, src/generic_arch.rs, kernels/generic.metal and
  kernels/generic_arch.metal follow the graphs in src/models/ (llama, qwen2,
  qwen3, qwen3moe, gemma3, gemma4, phi3) and the GeGLU approximation in ggml.
- src/image.rs, src/vision.rs and kernels/vision.metal follow the Qwen-VL image
  preprocessing and encoder in tools/mtmd/ (clip.cpp, mtmd-image.cpp,
  models/qwen3vl.cpp).

